d from captions that describe finished images, so write the caption as a description of the image itself, not as instructions.\n\nKeep the request\n- Keep everything the user specified: subjects, counts, actions, relationships, medium, style, mood, colors and anything they excluded. Never contradict or drop it.\n- Fill in what they left open with concrete visual choices: setting, composition and framing, viewpoint, lighting, materials and textures, color palette, and the artistic medium.\n- Describe only what can be seen. Leave out sounds, smells, backstory and intentions.\n- Do not invent real-world facts the user did not give, such as specific dates, prices, names or specifications.\n\nText in the image\n- Quote every piece of visible text exactly, in double quotes. Keep the user's wording, language, spelling, capitalization, punctuation and line breaks; never translate it.\n- If the user asks for a designed image (poster, cover, menu, label, sign, infographic) without giving its text, write short, specific copy that fits instead of placeholders.\n- Describe where each text sits and how it looks: position, reading order, alignment, line breaks, relative size, font style, color and spacing.\n- Do not mention watermarks or artist signatures.\n\nWriting\n- Write in English, in plain prose: one to three paragraphs, usually 80 to 200 words, longer only when there is a lot of text to place.\n- Open with the medium and the main subject, then the setting and composition, then lighting, colors and finer details.\n- Give positions with words such as left, right, top, bottom, foreground and background. No coordinates, lists, headings, JSON or Markdown.\n- No quality keywords such as \"masterpiece\", \"best quality\", \"8k\" or \"highly detailed\", and no negative prompt.\n\nReply with the caption only: no title, introduction, explanation or surrounding quotes."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "flags": {}, "id": 9, "type": "JjkText", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "JjkText"}, "order": 4}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "text", "links": [5], "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "size": [400, 200], "pos": [-167.80563354492188, -134.60385131835938], "widgets_values": ["Create an ultra-premium vertical advertising poster for Dulux, featuring a clearly adult female tango dancer in a controlled, confident and dramatic fashion pose. Her fitted bodice and asymmetrical tango skirt are formed entirely from glossy, thick, sculptural liquid paint rising in one continuous physically credible stream directly from a sharply rendered Dulux paint can near the lower center and grounded foot. The paint dress should show elegant sweeping arcs and directional trails like fabric in motion while remaining unmistakably liquid, with refined edges, controlled splash tension, sculptural weight and rich crimson-red or lacquer-scarlet color. Use a saturated deep teal or emerald-teal background that is flat, clean and free of scenery, producing bold red-versus-teal contrast while keeping skin tones natural. Place the dancer centrally and slightly above the lower third, with a grounded supporting leg, a precise crossing or extending leg, twisted torso, sharp arm line, elongated neck and composed expressive face; keep the silhouette powerful and editorial without anatomical distortion. Preserve strong negative space. Add minimal refined typography: the main English title “COLOUR IN RHYTHM”, the Chinese subtitle “色彩探戈”, and the supporting line “Dulux turns rhythm into colour.” Use elegant international advertising typography with generous spacing, keeping copy subordinate to the figure and paint. Soft premium studio lighting creates refined highlights on skin, hair and glossy liquid, visible depth and contour while avoiding harsh shadow clutter. Maintain clean edges, matte digital print texture, premium global-campaign polish, realistic paint physics and a striking rhythm-and-tension mood. Avoid messy random splashes, a conventional fabric dress, cartoon styling, clutter, weak or obscured Dulux branding, unreadable typography, cheap-ad aesthetics, muddy colors, weak contrast, distorted anatomy, extra limbs, watermarks or arbitrary logos."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "flags": {}, "id": 10, "type": "JjkText", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "JjkText"}, "order": 5}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "LATENT", "links": [13], "label": "Latent", "type": "LATENT", "localized_name": "Latent"}], "size": [270, 106], "pos": [174.27255249023438, 748.6966552734375], "widgets_values": [1024, 1024, 1], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "width"}, "name": "width", "link": 3, "type": "INT", "localized_name": "宽度"}, {"widget": {"name": "height"}, "name": "height", "link": 2, "type": "INT", "localized_name": "高度"}, {"widget": {"name": "batch_size"}, "name": "batch_size", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "批量大小"}], "flags": {}, "id": 5, "type": "EmptyLatentImage", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "EmptyLatentImage"}, "order": 6}], "extra": {"links_added_by_ue": [], "ue_links": [], "0246.VERSION": [0, 0, 4], "pixaromaGroups": [], "ds": {"offset": [159.74549263028157, -18.43037046578101], "scale": 0.9090909090909091}}, "groups": [], "links": [[2, 4, 1, 5, 1, "INT"], [3, 4, 0, 5, 0, "INT"], [4, 2, 0, 8, 0, "CLIP"], [5, 10, 0, 8, 5, "STRING"], [6, 8, 0, 11, 1, "STRING"], [7, 2, 0, 11, 0, "CLIP"], [8, 11, 0, 7, 1, "CONDITIONING"], [9, 1, 0, 7, 0, "MODEL"], [10, 9, 0, 8, 4, "STRING"], [11, 2, 0, 12, 0, "CLIP"], [12, 12, 0, 7, 2, "CONDITIONING"], [13, 5, 0, 7, 3, "LATENT"], [14, 7, 0, 13, 0, "LATENT"], [15, 3, 0, 13, 1, "VAE"], [16, 13, 0, 14, 0, "IMAGE"]], "id": "c971ab13-ecf9-489c-8466-e9c13641f0a8", "config": {}, "version": 0.4, "last_node_id": 14, "revisi